Disable rules_rust's hermetic macOS SDKROOT injection.

Since rules_rs 0.0.76, `rules_rust` defaults `rust_*` rules' `macos_sdkroot`
attribute to `@macos_sdk//sysroot` (the hermetic macOS SDK shipped by the
`@llvm` module). On macOS, `rust/private/rustc.bzl` then writes
`SDKROOT=${pwd}/external/llvm++osx+macos_sdk/sysroot` into every Rustc/link
action's env. At the same time, Bazel's apple `cc_toolchain`
(`apple_support`'s `local_config_apple_cc`) sets `APPLE_SDK_VERSION_OVERRIDE`,
which makes Bazel's `XcodeLocalEnvProvider.rewriteLocalEnv` also `put`
`SDKROOT=/Applications/Xcode.app/.../MacOSX*.sdk`. The two `SDKROOT` entries
then collide in `ImmutableMap.buildOrThrow()` and Bazel crashes; see
upstream bug https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/25438.

We don't need rules_rust's hermetic macOS SDK: the apple `cc_toolchain` from
`apple_support` already provides a working sysroot to clang at link time.
This patch makes `default_macos_sdkroot` resolve to the empty filegroup on
macOS too, so `_apple_sdkroot()` short-circuits to `None` and rules_rust
never injects `SDKROOT` into the action env.

--- a/rust/private/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/rust/private/BUILD.bazel
@@ -20,10 +20,11 @@ filegroup(
 
 alias(
     name = "default_macos_sdkroot",
-    actual = select({
-        "@platforms//os:osx": "@macos_sdk//sysroot",
-        "//conditions:default": ":empty_macos_sdkroot",
-    }),
+    # On macOS, apple_support's cc_toolchain already injects SDKROOT via
+    # Bazel's XcodeLocalEnvProvider. Pointing this at @macos_sdk//sysroot
+    # causes a duplicate-SDKROOT crash in XcodeLocalEnvProvider; see
+    # https://github.com/bazelbuild/bazel/issues/25438.
+    actual = ":empty_macos_sdkroot",
     visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
 )
 
